{"id":"769c4f46-148e-476f-8498-e8dc253be508","revision":0,"last_node_id":15,"last_link_id":12,"nodes":[{"id":15,"type":"Note","pos":[-930.5085707978384,-12663.906652725804],"size":[1043.2840508962831,1144.6620918693934],"flags":{"pinned":true},"order":0,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"title":"🏷️ NOVA AUDIO TAG READER","properties":{"ue_properties":{"widget_ue_connectable":{},"version":"7.8","input_ue_unconnectable":{}}},"widgets_values":["Reads the tags a folder of audio files actually carries, and prints\nthem. This template only reads. Nothing is written, moved or renamed.\n\n\n📁 1. POINT IT AT YOUR FOLDER\n-----------------------------\n\nNova Batch Load Audio > folder_path. Leave it empty to fall back to\nComfyUI's input/ folder. file_filter takes comma-separated globs (*.flac\nhere); empty matches every known audio extension. Turn on recursive if\nthe album sits in sub-folders.\n\n\n▶️ 2. RUN IT\n------------\n\nThree consoles, left to right:\n\n* File Names  (the batch in order, one line per file)\n* Metadata    (the scan record: what matched, what was skipped, warnings)\n* Tags        (the report, file by file)\n\n\n📝 WHY decode_audio IS OFF\n--------------------------\n\nThe tag nodes work on file paths and never look at a waveform. Decoding\na folder of FLACs just to read their tags costs minutes of CPU and\ngigabytes of RAM for a result nothing reads. With it off the audio\noutput is a one-sample silent placeholder, so don't wire it to a player\nand expect sound. Turn it on only when you want the batch as a tensor\nfor a masterer or analyser.\n\n\n⚙️ THE SETTINGS THAT MATTER HERE\n--------------------------------\n\n* limit = 0            (No cap. A non-zero value truncates the batch silently: no warning, no error)\n* max_value_chars = 0  (No truncation, which is why full lyric sheets print. Set 160 to keep the report                  skimmable. tags_json is complete either way)\n* show_missing = on    (A requested field the file doesn't carry is reported as missing. Off, it is silently omitted, which looks identical to a field you forgot to list. Leave it on)\n* fields               (tracknumber, title, artist, album, date, genre, comment, copyright, encodedby, lyrics. Use * to list every tag a file carries in its own order)\n\n\n🎵 MIXED FORMATS ARE FINE\n-------------------------\n\nID3 frames and MP4 atoms are reported under the names FLAC uses: TIT2\nand (c)nam both come back as title. One fields list works across the\nwhole folder.\n\n\n✅ TO VERIFY A WRITE\n--------------------\n\nNova Tag Writer passes its batch through unchanged, so Tag Writer >\nfiles > Tag Reader > console > Nova Console reads back what was just\nwritten, from disk, in the same run.\n\nRequires mutagen. Take tags_json rather than console if another node is\ngoing to consume the result."],"color":"#432","bgcolor":"#653"},{"id":11,"type":"NovaBatchLoadAudio","pos":[120.31529283852075,-12662.652051253317],"size":[422.05762770649017,258],"flags":{},"order":1,"mode":0,"inputs":[{"localized_name":"folder_path","name":"folder_path","type":"STRING","widget":{"name":"folder_path"},"link":null},{"localized_name":"file_filter","name":"file_filter","type":"STRING","widget":{"name":"file_filter"},"link":null},{"localized_name":"recursive","name":"recursive","type":"BOOLEAN","widget":{"name":"recursive"},"link":null},{"localized_name":"sort_by","name":"sort_by","type":"COMBO","widget":{"name":"sort_by"},"link":null},{"localized_name":"limit","name":"limit","type":"INT","widget":{"name":"limit"},"link":null},{"localized_name":"decode_audio","name":"decode_audio","type":"BOOLEAN","widget":{"name":"decode_audio"},"link":null}],"outputs":[{"localized_name":"files","name":"files","type":"NOVA_FILES","links":[9]},{"localized_name":"audio","name":"audio","type":"AUDIO","links":null},{"localized_name":"file_count","name":"file_count","type":"INT","links":null},{"localized_name":"filenames","name":"filenames","shape":6,"type":"STRING","links":[11]},{"localized_